          <circle cx="150" cy="30" r="6" fill="#36c7b5" />
          <text x="150" y="15" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="10" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">0800</text>
          
          <circle cx="450" cy="30" r="6" fill="#36c7b5" />
          <text x="450" y="15" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="10" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">2000</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
      <p class="infographic-caption">Figure 2: Infographic contrasting the distinct numbers used in the 24-hour clock vs standard time.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       SECTION 4: HOW MILITARY TIME WORKS
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="how-military-time-works" class="content-section reveal" aria-label="How Military Time Works">
    <h2>4. How Military Time Works</h2>
    <p>
      Military Time uses a clean, four-digit numeric format. The first two digits of the sequence represent the hour, and the final two digits represent the minutes. In traditional military usage, no colons or punctuation are used to separate the hours from the minutes.
    </p>
    <p>
      For example, 8:45 AM is written as **0845** (spoken as "zero eight forty-five"). Similarly, 6:15 PM is written as **1815** (spoken as "eighteen fifteen").
    </p>
    <p>
      In spoken military communication, time values are expressed as "hundred hours" when they fall exactly on the hour. For example, 10:00 AM is written as **1000** and spoken as "ten hundred hours." 10:00 PM is written as **2200** and spoken as "twenty-two hundred hours." If minutes are present, they are spoken sequentially without the word "hundred." For example, 10:15 AM is written as **1015** and spoken as "ten fifteen." 10:15 PM is written as **2215** and spoken as "twenty-two fifteen."
    </p>

    <!-- Custom Inline SVG: 24-hour clock wheel (Infographic 4) -->
    <div style="margin: 2.5rem 0; text-align: center; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--panel);">
